  "$comment": "Pickup items (sim/items.ts; map pickup entities name one by `id`, so never rename one). The order is MapMaker's palette order and the order random weapon pickups roll from (sim/pickupRoll.ts): add new ones at the end. No network code: pickups travel as their id. `effect.kind`: health / armor (`amount`), ammo (`ammo`: one ammo type, or leave it out for every owned weapon), throwable (`throwable`, `count`), weapon (`weapon`), powerup (`powerup` speed or damage, `seconds`), jetpack, glider, uav (`seconds`), disc (`power`). `displayName`: leave it out for a weapon pickup (the weapon's name) or a disc power (its label in sim/discs.ts). `respawnSeconds`: default respawn (a placed pickup can override it). `botValue`: what bots think it is worth (0-1, before the situation scales it); leave it out for a weapon pickup to get 0.55 + respawnSeconds / 120, at most 0.9 (power weapons respawn slower and are worth more). `rules`: armor (`max`, `absorb`: share of incoming damage armor takes while any is left), powerup multiples, pickup reach. Edit, then run `node tools/content/pickups.mjs`.",
